--- body ---
## Context

The XLSX editions 2024-q3 and 2025-q1 of the South African JET Grants
Register carry a "Financing Status" sheet, declared out of scope in parser
v1 ([[1950]], `XLSX_SCOPE_OUT` in `scripts/jetp/_zaf_grants_layouts.py`).
It is a hand-keyed pledge matrix in US$ millions:

- rows: sovereign partners (Canada, Denmark, EU/EIB, France/AFD,
  Germany/KfW, Netherlands, Spain, Switzerland, UK, US), then a
  multilateral block (AfDB, the CIF-led Accelerated Coal Transition line,
  World Bank), subtotals and "Total pledges";
- columns: Grants, Highly-concessional loans, Concessional loans,
  Commercial debt and equity, Export Credits, total; 2025-q1 adds Policy
  Loans, Guarantees and a ZAR column at 17.64 R/US$;
- total pledges 13,806 (2024-q3) and 12,832 (2025-q1); in 2025-q1 the US
  row is zeroed ("withdrawn"), Canada gains a 91 policy loan, Germany's
  concessional loans are re-split (1,548 into 748 plus 800 policy);
- 2024-q3 rows 18 and 19 carry unlabelled numbers (300, 30) belonging to
  the coal-transition line.

No Unique IDs and no grant rows: these are pledges, not allocations.

## Costing (assessment of 2026-10-01, not measured)

- Code: about 80 to 120 lines of a matrix reader in
  `_zaf_grants_layouts.py`, the sheet-to-ledger mapping in
  `build_zaf_grants_register.py`, a parser method version bump; the
  scope-out test (the out-of-scope set) changes.
- Tests: about 100 to 150 lines, with red tests of the new controls.
- Agent effort 4 to 6 h; author 2 to 3 h of decisions (below); USD 0.
- Controls: subtotals and "Total pledges" checked against the cells, an
  internal sum control. No cross-control with the grant rows: pledged
  grants (836m in 2024-q3, 764m in 2025-q1) legitimately exceed the
  allocated grant rows (about 630m, 583m); a cross-control would fail by
  design and a weakened one would mislead.
- Instruments map onto the finance-type list of [[1960]] through the
  reviewed crosswalk, hence the block.

## Author decisions needed (before any code)

1. What an envelope statement is here: one per partner × instrument cell,
   or one per partner total with the instruments as fields.
2. Sub-lines (the unlabelled 2024-q3 rows of the coal-transition line,
   footnotes): statements of their own, fields of their parent, or out of
   scope.
3. Whether the zeroed US row of 2025-q1 is read as a withdrawal statement
   (`absence` or an `event`) or only as a zero envelope.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Author decisions 1 to 3 logged here
- [ ] Matrix read for both XLSX editions under a new parser method version;
  internal sum controls pass or the publisher's inconsistency is declared
- [ ] Instruments mapped through the [[1960]] crosswalk, never by the reader
- [ ] Red tests; `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
